# Research in the Humanities: Ideals and Idols

**Authors:** Gombrich, E. H.

## Abstract
Research in the humanities should be done in areas of interest, under circumstances conducive to intellectual study and should not be undertaken for the purposes of gathering all information on a subject, for the purpose of seeking the novel, in order to apply the latest research tools, or totally because the subject is being taught and information is necessary. (Author/JB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ075361

